course: dictionary
lesson: 9206
title: Solder: joining metal with heat
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Solder is a soft metal mixture that melts at a low temperature. Melting means it turns from solid into liquid when it gets hot. Makers use it to join pieces of metal or wires together.
explain: Read the clues around the word. «An oven melts solder, a metal that melts easily, to fix them.» The sentence tells you solder melts easily, and it is used to fix tiny parts onto a board. Try your meaning in the sentence: "an oven melts a metal that joins things" still makes sense, so you are on the right track.
explain: As a verb, to solder means to join metal parts or wires using melted solder and a hot tool called a soldering iron. Pupils solder parts onto circuit boards to make a strong electrical connection. Safety comes first: the iron is over 300 °C, so wear goggles and work in air that moves.
fact: Solder is a metal mixture that melts at a low temperature.
fact: Solder can be a noun (the metal) or a verb (to join with it): «I solder the wires together.»
fact: A soldering iron is the hot tool that melts the solder so it can join the parts.
fact: The soldering iron is extremely hot, over 300 °C, so wear goggles and wash your hands afterwards.
fact: Phrases you will meet: «soldering iron», «solder a joint», «lead-free solder».
exercise: What is solder? | A wooden tool for cutting paper | A hot drink | A green board with copper tracks | *A soft metal mixture that melts at a low temperature
exercise: In «an oven melts solder, a metal that melts easily», what does melts mean? | Breaks into tiny pieces | Freezes into ice | Turns into a gas and disappears | *Turns from solid into liquid when it gets hot
exercise: Pupils solder components onto circuit boards. What does solder mean here? | To cut wires into short pieces | *To join metal parts or wires using melted solder | To cool down a hot metal | To paint a board green
test: What is the hot tool used to melt solder called? | A pair of scissors | A hammer | A screwdriver | *A soldering iron
test: Why must you be careful with a soldering iron? | It makes a loud noise | *It is extremely hot, over 300 °C | It is made of wood | It only works in the dark
exam: Which phrase means joining two wires with solder? | *Solder a joint | Bake the cake | Paint the board | Cut the wire
